-- title:
--   Full level 2: Γ_H(4M') field equals level-M' modular field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` for the residue field of the local ring $A$. Let `levelH q M'` be the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ on unit groups. The assertion is an equality of intermediate fields of $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$: the field `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, that is the $\kappa$-subfield of `LaurentSeries κ` generated by the set `intFormRatiosC κ Γ` attached to the congruence subgroup $\Gamma =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of `levelH q M'` under `gamma0Units (q ^ 2 * M')` on $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$, coincides with `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, the $\kappa$-subfield of `LaurentSeries κ` generated by the two Laurent series `jqModC κ` (the reduction into $\kappa$ of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot$`jNum` of $j$) and `jqNModC κ M' = qExpand κ M' (jqModC κ)`, i.e. $j(q^{M'})$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$2$ degeneration of the full level-$q$ structure: for $q = 2$ the level-$H$ $q$-expansion function field at level $4M'$ over the residue field of a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $2$ collapses to the level-$M'$ modular function field $\kappa(j(q), j(q^{M'}))$. It feeds the identification of places and integral models of the full-level modular curve in the case $q = 2$, used by the results on Igusa rings and uniqueness of the place extending a given $q$-expansion.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_xHFunctionFieldC_levelH_eq_modularFunctionFieldC_of_liesOverPrime_of_eq_two.lean

